cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "atomic-information-lab: exact value of information and optional stopping in a synthetic two-state measurement model"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Coworker Research / Coworkerz"
version: 0.1.0
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  Small dependency-free Python reference for Bayes-optimal adaptive measurement
  with an explicit STOP action in a synthetic discrete two-state model with
  unknown sensor inversion, measurement back-action, finite model uncertainty
  and a retention penalty. Verified against an independent exact oracle.
  No hardware, instrument or quantum claim.
keywords:
  - POMDP
  - optimal stopping
  - value of information
  - Brier score
